course: dictionary
lesson: 7183
title: Personification
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Personification means giving a thing that is not human a human action or feeling. «The wind howled.» Wind cannot howl like a dog or a person, but the word helps you picture the wind as if it were alive.
explain: «The sun smiled down on the village.» The sun has no face, so this gives it a happy, friendly feeling. The picture is warmer than just saying the sun was shining, and that is why poets use personification.
explain: Personification has a second meaning too. A personification of an idea is a person or character who stands for that idea. Father Time stands for time, and the statue of Justice holding scales is a personification of justice.
fact: Personification means giving human actions or feelings to things that are not human.
fact: «The wind screamed» and «the moon smiled» are both examples of personification.
fact: A personification can also be a person or character who stands for an idea, as in «Father Time is a personification of time».
fact: Poets often use personification together with similes, metaphors and alliteration.
fact: In Tennyson's poem «The Eagle», the line «He clasps the crag with crooked hands» gives an eagle hands, though an eagle has talons, so this is personification.
exercise: Which example shows personification? | The apple is red | The room was very cold | The dog ran home | *The sun smiled down on the fields
exercise: In «The leaves danced in the breeze», which word gives a human action to the leaves? | the | breeze | *danced | leaves
exercise: A statue of Justice holding scales is an example of what? | a question | an alliteration | a simile | *a personification
test: In «the wind screamed», what human action is given to the wind? | To whisper | To count | *To scream | To sleep
test: «Father Time is a personification of time.» What does this mean? | A clock that runs fast | *A person who stands for the idea of time | A time when children go to sleep | A type of poem
exam: Which is the best example of personification? | «The lamp was bright» | «The stars were like diamonds» | *«The moon watched over the sleeping village» | «The river was long and wide»
